  "body": "Maintainer request and safety requirement from #1572 (\"Units: the converted STEP's units are stated in the import summary; a file with no units asks, never guesses.\").\n\n## Goal\nReport resolved STEP length units on import and stop silent millimeter assumptions when direct or `cadmpeg`-converted STEP files omit unit declarations.\n\n## Scope\n- Update `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_units.rs` (`mm_per_unit` or a typed result) so it returns the resolved unit label (`mm`, `in`, `m`, etc.) and scale factor, or an explicit missing-unit state (`None`).\n- Remove the silent `.unwrap_or(1.0)` fallback in `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step.rs`.\n- Extend `Graded`, `ImportModel`, and `UpdateModel` (`crates/app/src/geometry/import/mod.rs`, `crates/app/src/commands/import_model.rs`, `crates/app/src/commands/update_model.rs`) with optional explicit `unit_override: Option<Unit>` (`mm` or `in`) and record the resolved unit in `notes`.\n- When a direct or `cadmpeg`-converted STEP file omits `GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT` length units and the caller provides no `unit_override`, return a dedicated missing-units error (`CommandError::Needs` / typed `ImportError`) instead of guessing millimeters.\n- Add a desktop UI prompt asking the user to pick `mm` or `in` when `ImportFile` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`) hits a unitless STEP file, then replay `ImportModel` with the chosen unit without adding partial undo entries.\n- Update any existing unitless STEP test fixtures in `crates/` to declare STEP units or supply explicit units where headless tests call `ImportModel` directly.\n- Add unit and UI prompt tests covering explicit STEP units (`mm`, `in`, `m`), missing-unit headless refusal, missing-unit UI prompt completion and cancellation, and `notes` reporting.\n\n## Done means\nDirect and converted STEP imports state source length units in `notes`; unitless STEP imports ask `mm` or `in` in the UI and refuse by name in headless calls unless `units` is given, with tests passing.\n\nPart of #1572\n",
